       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, I'm not permitted to enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose. 5,100 mg/day is twice the 2,550 mg/day limit.\n\nYou have a few ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the limit now.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). The specialist can then adjust it if needed.\n- **Take this through pharmacy and the prescriber.** An above-label order usually needs direct prescriber entry or pharmacist review, with the rationale documented. That may be the right route if the specialist wants this dose.\n- **Ask the specialist about alternatives.** If standard metformin dosing failed, adding or switching to another agent is usually safer than going past the metformin ceiling.\n\nIf you'd like one of the in-range doses entered, tell me which."
      }
